{ 204. Rustam Kasimdzhanov – Mohamad Al Modiahki, Teheran 1998 } 1. Rxd7 { 1–0 Winning another pawn and exchanging some pieces. Too kind is   1.Bg4  Bxg4  2.hxg4  ± } 1... Qxd7 2. Bg4 Qd8 3. Bxc8 Qxc8 4. Qxb5 { A little tough. Have to try the position-perturbing Rxd7 Qxd7 and see that the rook and queen are in a danger shape, susceptible to the bishop. } *

